menu "BlueAudio Puck: buttons and LED"

    config PUCK_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Main button GPIO (-1 if not fitted)"
        default 33
        range -1 39
        help
            Wired to ground through the switch; the internal pull-up holds it
            high when open. GPIO 33 is also an RTC pin, so it can wake the chip
            from deep sleep later.

    config PUCK_VOLUME_UP_GPIO
        int "Volume up button GPIO (-1 if not fitted)"
        default -1
        range -1 39
        help
            Optional. Volume normally comes from the phone over AVRCP, so this
            is only needed if you want the puck itself to have volume keys.

    config PUCK_VOLUME_DOWN_GPIO
        int "Volume down button GPIO (-1 if not fitted)"
        default -1
        range -1 39

    config PUCK_LED_GPIO
        int "Status LED GPIO (-1 if not fitted)"
        default -1
        range -1 33
        help
            Driven by LEDC PWM so the LED can breathe and dim rather than only
            blink. Must be an output-capable pin: GPIO 34-39 are input only.

            Defaults to "not fitted" because GPIO 2 -- the on-board LED on most
            devkits -- now carries I2S data. An external LED on a free pin such
            as 27 works; with the OLED fitted the LED is largely redundant
            anyway, since the screen shows the same states in words.

    config PUCK_LED_ACTIVE_LOW
        bool "Status LED is active low"
        default n
        help
            Enable if the LED is wired between the pin and 3V3 rather than
            between the pin and ground.

    config PUCK_VOLUME_STEP
        int "Volume change per button press"
        default 8
        range 1 32
        help
            In AVRCP units, where full scale is 127. 8 gives 16 steps across
            the range.

endmenu
